    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 2nd centers on three primary anchors who clear the 60.0 efficiency threshold. **Jackson Merrill** (62.07) stands as our top play, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Nola yields significant upside, even with the modest penalty for elite hold/SB risk. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.14) remains a must-start despite a wind-in factor at the park, as his high xwOBA remains the most reliable foundation for our daily run production. Additionally, **Kyle Tucker** (61.08) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.04) provide elite efficiency; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically benefits from a favorable matchup against the right-handed Bachar, where his platoon splits provide the necessary ceiling to justify a high-leverage start. \n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who sat just outside the active lineup with a 48.16 score. While **Coby Mayo** presents a legitimate threat, the optimizer favored **Josh Jung** and **Miguel Vargas** due to their projected top-of-the-order involvement and specific park-factor advantages. We are monitoring the status of **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Kyle Tucker** closely, as their scores are currently based on projected lineups; any shift toward the bottom of the order would necessitate a downward revision in their efficiency scores. We continue to manage our daily game caps carefully, evidenced by the decision to bench **Brayan Rocchio** (35.70), who failed to meet our 40.0 baseline, and holding the injured **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL until further notice.",
